From b0e2b2839260d73cdf3b5afa0900abb331137fd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yinvoker <yinvoker@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:52:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] patch: order RequestSentences by request id, not by heap
 address
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RequestSentence::operator< compared the Ptr<Request> smart pointers when
the sentences belong to different requests, so the batching pool's
std::set ordered same-length sentences by allocator addresses. Batch
membership then varied run to run (and pass to pass), which changed each
batch's shortlist union and with it the logits — the source of the
pass-level nondeterminism seen in the perf experiments (0-3 flipped
sentences per 150 with shortlist on; fully stable with shortlist off,
where the row-independent full-vocab output makes membership invisible).

Dereference and compare the Requests themselves: Request::operator<
orders by the service's monotonic sequence id, i.e. arrival order.

Verified on host (en-zh, FLORES-150, shortlist on): 5 passes x 3
processes (incl. MallocPreScribble) hash-identical for blocking; 5
passes x 2 runs identical for 2 and 4 workers; the stable output is one
of the variants the unfixed code already produced, and timing is
unchanged. Upstream mozilla/translations main carries the same
comparator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engine/src/translator/request.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engine/src/translator/request.cpp b/engine/src/translator/request.cpp
index fd8fe8f..729bf86 100644
--- a/engine/src/translator/request.cpp
+++ b/engine/src/translator/request.cpp
@@ -112,7 +112,11 @@ bool operator<(const RequestSentence &a, const RequestSentence &b) {
   if (a.request_ == b.request_) {
     return a.index_ < b.index_;
   }
-  return a.request_ < b.request_;
+  // Compare the Requests (by sequence id), not the smart pointers: ordering by
+  // heap address made the batching pool's std::set traversal - and therefore
+  // batch membership, the per-batch shortlist union and ultimately the
+  // translations - depend on allocator state, varying run to run.
+  return *a.request_ < *b.request_;
 }
 
